#N Glider
#C The smallest spaceship. Travels one cell diagonally every four generations,
#C which makes it the clearest probe for the 2^64 seam: its displacement is
#C exactly predictable, so an incorrect wrap shows as a wrong position rather
#C than a plausible-looking mess.
#C Positioned two cells before the wrap point, so it crosses the seam within
#C four generations. Pos is the signed reading of the same 64 bits.
#CXRLE Pos=-2,-2
x = 3, y = 3, rule = B3/S23
bo$2bo$3o!
